      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T13:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Clone a fresh Gerrit repo\n\n2. Run `npm run eslintfix`\n\n3. Notice this error\n```\nERROR: Skipping \u0027polygerrit-ui/app:lint_bin\u0027: error loading package \u0027polygerrit-ui/app\u0027: Unable to find package for @@[unknown repo \u0027build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 requested from @@]//:index.bzl: The repository \u0027@@[unknown repo \u0027build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 requested from @@]\u0027 could not be resolved: No repository visible as \u0027@build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 from main repository.\nERROR: error loading package \u0027polygerrit-ui/app\u0027: Unable to find package for @@[unknown repo \u0027build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 requested from @@]//:index.bzl: The repository \u0027@@[unknown repo \u0027build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 requested from @@]\u0027 could not be resolved: No repository visible as \u0027@build_bazel_rules_nodejs\u0027 from main repository.\nINFO: Elapsed time: 0.148s\nINFO: 0 processes.\nERROR: Build did NOT complete successfully\nERROR: Build failed. Not running target\n```\n\n4. Ask Gemini to fix this and arrive at this change",
      "parentUuid": "0d8f8c38_c77c2064",
      "revId": "ae356b4c27a5d607d600ffe93609843e2e2d7153",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2747d834_ed07ba74",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1083225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T14:02:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nThis error message from Bazel indicates that it cannot find the definition for the external repository named @build_bazel_rules_nodejs. This repository contains the rules necessary to build, test, and work with Node.js projects within a Bazel workspace.\n\nThe specific error means that a BUILD or .bzl file (in this case, //:index.bzl as referenced from polygerrit-ui/app) is trying to load() something from @build_bazel_rules_nodejs, but this repository hasn\u0027t been declared in your Bazel WORKSPACE file.\n\nHow to Fix:\n\nYou need to define the @build_bazel_rules_nodejs external repository in the WORKSPACE file located at the root of your Bazel project. You can do this using the http_archive rule.\n\n```\n\nThis was it\u0027s thinking",
      "parentUuid": "f4c92987_6be4e0a0",
      "revId": "ae356b4c27a5d607d600ffe93609843e2e2d7153",
